{
 "slug": "html_colors",
 "course": "html",
 "order": 11,
 "url": "/html/html_colors.asp",
 "title": "HTML Colors",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h1",
   "text": "HTML Colors"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "HTML colors are specified with predefined color names, or with\nRGB, HEX, HSL, RGBA, or HSLA values."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Color Names"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "In HTML, a color can be specified by using a color name:"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Tomato"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Orange"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "DodgerBlue"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "MediumSeaGreen"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Gray"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "SlateBlue"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Violet"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "LightGray"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Try it Yourself »"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "HTML supports 140 standard color names."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Background Color"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "You can set the background color for HTML elements:"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Hello World"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<h1 style=\"background-color:DodgerBlue;\">Hello World</h1>\n<p style=\"background-color:Tomato;\">Lorem\n  ipsum...</p>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_color_background"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Text Color"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "You can set the color of text:"
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Hello World"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetuer adipiscing elit, sed diam nonummy nibh euismod tincidunt ut laoreet dolore magna aliquam erat volutpat."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Ut wisi enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exerci tation ullamcorper suscipit lobortis nisl ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<h1 style=\"color:Tomato;\">Hello\n  World</h1>\n<p style=\"color:DodgerBlue;\">Lorem\n  ipsum...</p>\n<p style=\"color:MediumSeaGreen;\">Ut wisi\n  enim...</p>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_color_text"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Border Color"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "You can set the color of borders:"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Hello World"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Hello World"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Hello World"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<h1 style=\"border:2px\n  solid Tomato;\">Hello\n  World</h1>\n<h1 style=\"border:2px\n  solid DodgerBlue;\">Hello\n  World</h1>\n<h1 style=\"border:2px\n  solid Violet;\">Hello\n  World</h1>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_color_border"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Color Values"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "In HTML, colors can also be specified using RGB values, HEX values, HSL\nvalues, RGBA values, and HSLA values."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The following three <div> elements have their background color set with RGB,\nHEX, and HSL values:"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "rgb(255, 99, 71)"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "#ff6347"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "hsl(9, 100%, 64%)"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The following two <div> elements have their background color set with RGBA\nand HSLA values, which add an Alpha channel to the color (here we have 50%\ntransparency):"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "rgba(255, 99, 71, 0.5)"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "hsla(9, 100%, 64%, 0.5)"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<h1 style=\"background-color:rgb(255,\n  99, 71);\">...</h1>\n<h1 style=\"background-color:#ff6347;\">...</h1>\n<h1 style=\"background-color:hsl(9,\n  100%, 64%);\">...</h1>\n\n<h1 style=\"background-color:rgba(255,\n  99, 71, 0.5);\">...</h1>\n<h1 style=\"background-color:hsla(9,\n  100%, 64%, 0.5);\">...</h1>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_color_values"
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "variant": "note",
   "text": "Learn more about Color Values\nYou will learn more about RGB, HEX and HSL in the next chapters."
  }
 ]
}